NAME:
   dn-tool - enroll and unenroll Linux hosts in a defined.net Managed Nebula network

USAGE:
   dn-tool [global options] [command [command options]]

VERSION:
   $VERSION

COMMANDS:
   install       download and verify dnclient into the binary directory
   enroll        create the remote host record and run dnclient enroll
   unenroll      delete the remote host record and remove local config
   run           install, enroll, then run dnclient; unenroll on termination
   write-config  persist the current environment configuration to a 0600 file
   schema        print the machine-readable command, exit-code and error surface
   help, h       Shows a list of commands or help for one command

GLOBAL OPTIONS:
   --env-file FILE                    load configuration from key-value FILE [$DN_ENV_FILE]
   --assert-changed                   exit non-zero (distinct, non-error) when the command makes no change
   --log-level error|warn|info|debug  diagnostic verbosity on stderr: error|warn|info|debug (default: "warn")
   --quiet                            log only errors; overrides --log-level
   --help, -h                         show help
   --version, -v                      print the version
